## 5.6 Hierarchical MARL (H-MARL)

Hierarchical MARL abstracts extended temporal dependencies into high-level macro-actions or subgoals. H-MARL allows credit to bypass the low-level step-by-step decay of GAE. We propose the CHARM architecture. It isolates spatial and temporal dependencies into a two-tiered hierarchy. CHARM bridges the causal delay between upstream enablers and downstream outcomes. We benchmark CHARM against MAHIRO, ROMA, and LRS. A hierarchical causal approach solves the Stage 4 facility.
